1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
NASA data in, decisions out: detect, confirm, adapt, then test the trend

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:05,200
WHY: fires, floods, worn-out soil. The evidence is split across sensors.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,800
WHAT: three working modules feed one trend engine

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,700
DETECT: 11.6M NASA fire detections, one 2000–2025 record

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:15,100
Canada's fire detections: +3,019 a year since 2003 (p = 0.035)

6
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:18,000
CONFIRM: radar sees the Valencia flood through the clouds

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,300
Valencia's wettest-day rain: no trend (p = 0.28). Water storage: falling (p = 0.002)

8
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,300
ADAPT: rank crop rotations by a farmer's own priorities

9
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,300
Iowa's frost-free season: +0.43 days a year, later autumn frost (p = 0.006)

10
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,200
Every trend shows its slope, 95% CI and p-value. Live now.
